--                               already run. contract.test.ts:3763 asserts the
--                               string is in 012, which stays true.
--
-- Client:
--   src/api/provider.ts:378     useSetAvailability writes it. DELETE the hook.
--   src/api/chat.ts:137         `.order('is_available', ...)` becomes
--                               `.order('is_open', ...)`.
--   src/screens/ProviderHomeScreen.tsx:196
--                               `profile?.is_available ?? false` and the
--                               AVAILABILITY copy block. This file owns the
--                               toggle row. NOT owned by this change set.
--   src/lib/database.types.ts:101,401,467
--                               Profile.is_available, ProviderSummary
--                               .is_available, ConversationSummary
--                               .peer_available.
--   src/lib/languagePrefs.ts:164, src/lib/presence.ts:6,
--   src/components/ProviderRow.tsx:394, src/components/Avatar.tsx:268
--                               comments only.
--
-- Edge functions:                none. No function reads is_available.
--
-- pgTAP fixtures that SET it (they only need the line deleted):
--   060, 110:181, 160, 190, 240, 250:92, 260, 280, 290, 300, 340, 350, 360,
--   370, 380.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- THE QUESTION FOR AMIT, because the docs do not answer it
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- With the CHECK gone, a provider can be listed in the directory while offering
-- nothing. Today `is_available = false` does not hide them either, so this is
-- not a regression. But it is the moment to decide whether a closed provider
-- should be hidden from the directory entirely (add `and (p.chat_enabled or
-- p.audio_enabled or p.video_enabled)` to the WHERE above), sorted last, or
-- shown with a "not taking anyone new" state on the row. Sorting last is what
-- this file does, because it is what is_available does now and it changes
-- nothing anybody can see.
